**Note:** This is a simplified mental map. Generative AI and LLMs should not be treated as completely separate levels in a strict hierarchy. They describe different kinds of AI systems and capabilities.

## Five Important Distinctions

### 1. AI vs Traditional Rule-Based Programming

Traditional programs follow rules that are explicitly written by a programmer. AI is a broader field and can include systems that use rules as well as systems that learn patterns from data.

### 2. AI vs Machine Learning

AI and Machine Learning are not the same thing. AI is the broader field, while Machine Learning is one approach used to create AI systems by learning patterns from data.

### 3. Machine Learning vs Deep Learning

Machine Learning includes different methods for learning patterns from data. Deep Learning is a part of Machine Learning that uses neural networks with multiple layers.

### 4. Deep Learning vs Generative AI

Deep Learning describes a type of Machine Learning method. Generative AI describes systems whose main purpose is to generate new content such as text, images or code. Many modern Generative AI systems use Deep Learning.

### 5. Generative AI vs LLM

Generative AI can create different kinds of content such as text, images, audio or code. An LLM mainly works with language and can understand and generate text. Therefore, LLMs are an important type of modern Generative AI system, but Generative AI is broader than only LLMs.

## Explicitly Programmed vs Learned From Data

In traditional programming, a programmer directly writes the rules that decide what the program should do.

For example:

```text
IF temperature > 80°C
    Display WARNING
```

The computer does not learn this rule. The programmer created it.

In Machine Learning, instead of writing every possible rule, we provide examples and data. The ML system learns patterns from those examples and uses the learned model to make predictions on new data.

## Three Examples

| Example | Classification | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| Temperature warning: if temperature > 80°C, show WARNING | Rule-based software | The condition is directly written by the programmer and nothing is learned from data. |
| Gmail spam detection | Machine Learning | The system can learn patterns from examples of spam and non-spam emails and use those patterns to classify new emails. |
| ChatGPT generating an email | Generative AI / LLM | It generates new language based on the user's prompt. |

## What I Learned

Before learning this topic, I mainly thought AI and Machine Learning meant almost the same thing. Now I understand that AI is the larger field and Machine Learning is only one way of building AI systems. I also understood that automation does not automatically mean AI because a normal program can automate a task using fixed rules without learning anything from data.
